# HR Nexus on Vercel — environment reference for the EDUK8U deployment.
#
# This file is a template. It contains no real values and never should: every
# entry below is set in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables), or passed on the command line for the one-time database setup.
# Nothing here is read at runtime.
#
# WHICH VARIABLES THE RUNTIME ACTUALLY NEEDS
#
# Only the first group. The setup group is used once, from your own machine,
# against the hosted database - the deployed server never reads those, so
# putting them in Vercel is unnecessary.

# --------------------------------------------------------------- the runtime
# The hosted Postgres connection string, read by backend/src/config/db.ts. The
# server refuses to start without it. A Neon URL already ends in
# ?sslmode=require, which node-postgres honours; keep that on the end.
DATABASE_URL=replace-with-hosted-postgres-url

# Signs sign-in tokens. Generate a fresh one, for example:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
# Do not reuse the local development secret.
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-long-random-secret

# How long a sign-in lasts.
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d

# Only used to set the CORS origin (backend/src/app.ts). On Vercel the browser
# calls /api on the same origin it loaded the page from, so no CORS applies and
# this can be left unset for the first deployment. Set it afterwards only if you
# ever serve the frontend from a different domain than the API.
# FRONTEND_URL=https://your-project.vercel.app

# Where profile photographs are written. A serverless host cannot write next to
# its own code, so without this the server starts but refuses photographs, and
# anything it did accept would vanish on the next deployment. Point it at the
# host's temporary directory to accept them for the life of one instance, or
# leave it unset and leave photographs turned off.
# PROFILE_IMAGE_DIR=/tmp/profile-images

# ----------------------------------------------------------- the build input
# Makes the built frontend call /api on its own origin instead of the local
# development fallback. Set it for the frontend service.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# ------------------------------------- one-time setup, from your own machine
# These three are the same hosted Postgres URL. They are separate variables on
# purpose: each script refuses to fall back to the application's own database,
# so pointing a migration or a data load at the wrong place takes a deliberate
# act rather than a forgotten export.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=replace-with-same-hosted-postgres-url
EDUK8U_DATABASE_URL=replace-with-same-hosted-postgres-url

# The permanent review account. The .invalid suffix is reserved by RFC 2606 and
# can never be a real mailbox, which is what you want until you decide to use a
# real one.
EDUK8U_ADMIN_EMAIL=hr.review@eduk8u.invalid

# Chosen by you, passed to the bootstrap once, and stored only as a bcrypt hash.
# The account must change it at first sign-in, so this value stops working the
# moment anybody uses it. Never commit it.
EDUK8U_ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-with-your-own-password
